35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,The firms say the clay is tricky. But the depot notes say we can keep the park open.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The data is clear. The ground is thirsty and the people are rushing. We must design for flow.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found the names. The volunteers are already there, but the paid staff is very small. It feels fragile.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The eastern avenue trees died because no one watered them. The drawings promised life, but the contract promised nothing.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The ledger is heavy. Planting costs three times more to keep than paving. The fund only pays for the plants, not the paths.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Minako, if the trees died, does that mean the new plan will fail too?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, not if we stop fighting the water. The heat readings show the soil is already stressed.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"I am worried. If the volunteers leave, who is left? The casual pool is not enough for the whole year.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"It means we judge by the scars, not the sketches. The last decade shows us what happens when we ignore the upkeep.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree with Minako. The fund covers the green, but the city pays for the grey. That is a trap.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,I think we can work with the clay if we phase it right. The depot notes are our friend.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"The crossings show people want speed. We need hard paths, not soft lawns, in the main corridors.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,I like the idea of the volunteers helping. But I need to know if they are tired. Are they happy?,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,I am stubborn. I will not accept a plan that looks good on paper but rots in the ground.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,I am listening. The numbers say we must be careful. We cannot afford to be beautiful and broke.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I feel hopeful. We can do this if we listen to the ground and the people.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I am calm. The logic is sound. We design for the rain and the rush. That is the way.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I am a little sad, but also curious. I hope the new plan brings more friends to the park.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,I am ready. Let us see the candidates. I will look for the one that survives the second summer.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I am ready. The silence is comfortable. Let us see what remains when the noise stops.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
