60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,Option A looks like it works with the clay. The water stays where it belongs.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, yes. The drainage data supports A. The heat readings show the water will cool the air.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minato,,I like the quiet of the Woodland Walk. But who will clear the leaves? The volunteers are already busy.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Minako,,Option A is the only one that respects the ground. The others are just concrete waiting to crack.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,The fund pays for the planting in A. The city pays for the boardwalks. It is the most honest split.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,I am worried about the boardwalks. Will they hold up? The firms said the ground is soft.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the boardwalks are raised. They do not fight the ground. They float above it. It is logical.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minato,,I am thinking about the volunteers. They like the habitat tasks. Option A gives them something to do.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Minako,,I have seen the eastern avenue fail. Option A has a maintenance plan that includes watering. It is different.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"I am quiet, but I see the value. The long-term cost is lower because the fund covers the green.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I think Option A is the best. It works with the site, not against it.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I agree. The data points to A. The people cross the site, but the water stays. It is balanced.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I am a little nervous, but I like the idea of the ponds. It feels peaceful. I hope the volunteers are happy.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Minako,,I am confident. Option A is the one that will still be standing in ten years. The others are just drawings.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I am at peace. The numbers make sense. The fund covers the plants, and the city covers the paths. It is fair.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I am ready to vote. I believe in the water.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I am ready. Logic and nature align here. Let us choose the path that flows.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minato,,I am ready. I hope the new park is kind to the people who care for it.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Minako,,I am ready. I have seen the scars. I choose the plan that heals.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I am ready. The silence is full of promise. Let us choose the quiet strength.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
